{"name":"Baked Sienna","hex":"#9b775e","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"baked","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of bake"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["That has been cooked by baking.","Inebriated: drunk, high, or stoned."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/baked"},{"term":"sienna","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A form of clay containing iron and manganese.","A pigment with a reddish-brown colour."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["having a reddish-brown colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sienna"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sienna","blocks":[{"text":"Sienna is an earth pigment containing iron oxide and manganese oxide. In its natural state, it is yellowish brown, and it is called raw sienna. When heated, it becomes a reddish brown, and it is called burnt sienna. It takes its name from the city-state of Siena, where it was produced during the Renaissance. Along with ochre and umber, it was one of the first pigments to be used by humans, and is found in many cave paintings. Since the Renaissance, it has been one of the brown pigments most widely used by artists."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sienna"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Monteriggioni0001.jpg/120px-Monteriggioni0001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Monteriggioni0001.jpg/250px-Monteriggioni0001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Monteriggioni0001.jpg/120px-Monteriggioni0001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMonteriggioni0001.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/LimoniteUSGOV.jpg/120px-LimoniteUSGOV.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/LimoniteUSGOV.jpg/250px-LimoniteUSGOV.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/LimoniteUSGOV.jpg/120px-LimoniteUSGOV.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALimoniteUSGOV.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Hematite.jpg/120px-Hematite.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Hematite.jpg/250px-Hematite.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Hematite.jpg/120px-Hematite.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHematite.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Giorgio_Vasari_-_The_battle_of_Marciano_in_Val_di_Chiana_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/120px-Giorgio_Vasari_-_The_battle_of_Marciano_in_Val_di_Chiana_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Giorgio_Vasari_-_The_battle_of_Marciano_in_Val_di_Chiana_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/250px-Giorgio_Vasari_-_The_battle_of_Marciano_in_Val_di_Chiana_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Giorgio_Vasari_-_The_battle_of_Marciano_in_Val_di_Chiana_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/120px-Giorgio_Vasari_-_The_battle_of_Marciano_in_Val_di_Chiana_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail